      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "1. We need to find the average number of rounds played by each golfer.\n1. The chart provided shows the number of golfers who played different numbers of rounds of golf.\n1. To find the average, we need to add up the total number of rounds played by all the golfers and divide by the total number of golfers.\n1. We can count the number of golfers who played each number of rounds and add them up.\n    - 1 round: 5 golfers = 5 rounds\n    - 2 rounds: 2 golfers\n    - 3 rounds: 2 golfers\n    - 4 rounds: 3 golfers\n    - 5 rounds: 5 golfers\n1. We now have a list of the total number of rounds played by each number of rounds.\n1. We add up this list = 5 rounds + 2 rounds + 2 rounds + 3 rounds + 5 rounds = 17 rounds\n1. Finally, we divide by the number of golfers, total = 17 rounds / 15 golfers = 1.13 rounds per round\n1. Rounded to the nearest whole number, this is $\\boxed{1}.$",
